expected_issues.description:
`workgroupSizeX/Y/Z` are interpolated into WGSL without explicit `u32()` casts. If these values can be non-integers or expressions, WGSL may reject the shader. Consider ensuring they are integers in JS (see previous comment) and/or wrapping with `u32(...)` in the generated WGSL for the `instanceIndex` math to match `globalId`/`numWorkgroups` types.

```suggestion
@compute @workgroup_size( ${workgroupSizeX}, ${workgroupSizeY}, ${workgroupSizeZ} )
fn main( ${shaderData.attributes} ) {

	// system
	instanceIndex = globalId.x
		+ globalId.y * ( u32(${workgroupSizeX}) * numWorkgroups.x )
		+ globalId.z * ( u32(${workgroupSizeX}) * numWorkgroups.x ) * ( u32(${workgroupSizeY}) * numWorkgroups.y );
```

